              "elements": [
                {
                  "id": "0cd0ff49",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "heading",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Subheading",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-subheading",
                    "title": "The book and the brief",
                    "header_size": "h2"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "7f6f89b5",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "text-editor",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Copy",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-copy",
                    "editor": "<figure class=\"gp-case-evidence\"><img src=\"{{asset:my-dear-grandfather-302.webp}}\" width=\"302\" height=\"466\" alt=\"My Dear Grandfather cover, by Barsha Rai\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Supplied book cover. Cover design was not part of this listing project.</figcaption></figure><dl class=\"gp-case-facts\"><div><dt>Author</dt><dd>Barsha Rai</dd></div><div><dt>Client / publisher</dt><dd>Cactus Rain Publishing, owned by Nadine Laman</dd></div><div><dt>Marketplace</dt><dd>Amazon US</dd></div><div><dt>Editions reviewed</dt><dd>Kindle and paperback</dd></div><div><dt>Paperback</dt><dd>5.5 × 8.5 inches · 302 pages</dd></div><div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>Book description, keyword research and category review</dd></div></dl><p>The novel is set in Nepal. Rick’s relationship with his ailing grandfather sits within a story of family conflict, a murder and a missing family member. The listing needed to introduce that story clearly before moving into information about the author.</p>"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
