                    "title": "The challenge and what was observed",
                    "header_size": "h2"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "b8f340ee",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "text-editor",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Copy",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-copy",
                    "editor": "<p>The original Kindle-page material mixed story information and author biography in a dense block. A reader had to work to separate the novel’s premise from the background information. The visible category breadcrumb was useful as a starting point for research, but did not establish the complete backend setup.</p><figure class=\"gp-case-evidence\"><img src=\"{{asset:grandfather-original-kindle-767.webp}}\" width=\"767\" height=\"340\" alt=\"Original supplied Kindle listing screenshot, with story and author information in one dense description\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Original Kindle listing screenshot supplied in the case-study PDF, page 2. This is the starting-point evidence, not a matched paperback comparison.</figcaption></figure><p>The audit reported no visible Best Sellers Rank at that stage. That observation did not establish sales volume, advertising performance or the reasons for the listing’s visibility.</p>"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
