              "elements": [
                {
                  "id": "ae1d7390",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "heading",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Subheading",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-subheading",
                    "title": "Diagnosis and strategy",
                    "header_size": "h2"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "0a380bcc",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "text-editor",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Copy",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-copy",
                    "editor": "<p>The priority was to make the book’s story and positioning easier to understand. Description work brought the central situation and family tension forward. Keyword research considered relevant search language; category research explored possible routes for a mystery with a strong family element.</p><p>The research recommendations and the categories later visible on Amazon are different records. The report proposed Amateur Sleuth, Domestic and Murder options. The later supplied paperback record showed Aging Parents (Books), Traditional Detective Mysteries (Books) and Family Saga Fiction. We do not present those visible placements as proof that every recommended category was selected.</p>"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
