                {
                  "id": "bdc1bbf1",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "heading",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Subheading",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-subheading",
                    "title": "Observable outcomes and important limits",
                    "header_size": "h2"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                },
                {
                  "id": "2933fc23",
                  "elType": "widget",
                  "widgetType": "text-editor",
                  "isInner": false,
                  "settings": {
                    "_title": "Copy",
                    "_css_classes": "gp-copy",
                    "editor": "<p>The project produced a clearer description approach, documented keyword and category research, and a practical handover. The case-study source includes a later paperback ranking record: #2,936,816 in Books; #3,514 in Aging Parents; #16,588 in Traditional Detective Mysteries; and #18,156 in Family Saga Fiction.</p><p><strong>Those figures are a recorded snapshot, not a performance claim.</strong> Its date was not supplied. The earlier evidence concerned Kindle and the later record concerned paperback. They are not a matched before-and-after comparison, and neither proves that the optimisation caused sales or ranking changes.</p><p>No verified sales increase, advertising return, final Kindle category paths or saved backend keyword selections were provided. The case study does not establish platform approval or a guaranteed discovery outcome.</p>"
                  },
                  "elements": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
